Subject: Mapbox MCP SDK output validation warns instead of throwing (SDK 1.32.0)
Origin: DHI-internal (mapbox-mcp npm overlay)
Reference: https://github.com/mapbox/mcp-server/blob/v0.16.0/patches/@modelcontextprotocol%2Bsdk%2B1.30.0.patch
Description: Mapbox mcp-server carries a patch-package overlay so MCP tool output schema validation logs warnings instead of failing the request. The image pins @modelcontextprotocol/sdk at 1.32.0 via npm-bump.json and replaces the upstream 1.30.0 patch file after removing it from the checkout.
Base-Tree: tarball https://registry.npmjs.org/@modelcontextprotocol/sdk/-/sdk-1.32.0.tgz sha256:41dd4776a00ed50eaaa43ee335e27363ad1f53c3b7fa27fd0f75c0520f5342ec
Adaptation: Regenerated patch-package hunks for SDK 1.32.0 dist/cjs and dist/esm server/mcp.js with the same behavioral change as the Mapbox v0.16.0 patch against SDK 1.30.0.
Forwarded: not-needed (DHI overlay refresh for the image SDK pin; Mapbox upstream patch targets SDK 1.30.0)
Drop-When: never: Mapbox mcp-server still documents this patch-package behavior for tool output validation
Verify: cmd `dhi def build --fast image/mapbox-mcp/debian-13/0.yaml` expect "@modelcontextprotocol/sdk@1.32.0"

diff --git a/node_modules/@modelcontextprotocol/sdk/dist/cjs/server/mcp.js b/node_modules/@modelcontextprotocol/sdk/dist/cjs/server/mcp.js
index 8b43d01..525c619 100644
--- a/node_modules/@modelcontextprotocol/sdk/dist/cjs/server/mcp.js
+++ b/node_modules/@modelcontextprotocol/sdk/dist/cjs/server/mcp.js
@@ -241,15 +241,20 @@ class McpServer {
             return;
         }
         if (!result.structuredContent) {
-            throw new types_js_1.McpError(types_js_1.ErrorCode.InvalidParams, `Output validation error: Tool ${toolName} has an output schema but no structured content was provided`);
+            // Log warning but don't throw - allow tools to omit structured content
+            console.warn(`[MCP SDK Patch] Output validation warning: Tool ${toolName} has an output schema but no structured content was provided`);
         }
-        // if the tool has an output schema, validate structured content
-        const outputObj = (0, zod_compat_js_1.normalizeObjectSchema)(tool.outputSchema);
-        const parseResult = await (0, zod_compat_js_1.safeParseAsync)(outputObj, result.structuredContent);
-        if (!parseResult.success) {
-            const error = 'error' in parseResult ? parseResult.error : 'Unknown error';
-            const errorMessage = (0, zod_compat_js_1.getParseErrorMessage)(error);
-            throw new types_js_1.McpError(types_js_1.ErrorCode.InvalidParams, `Output validation error: Invalid structured content for tool ${toolName}: ${errorMessage}`);
+        else {
+            // if the tool has an output schema, validate structured content
+            const outputObj = (0, zod_compat_js_1.normalizeObjectSchema)(tool.outputSchema);
+            const parseResult = await (0, zod_compat_js_1.safeParseAsync)(outputObj, result.structuredContent);
+            if (!parseResult.success) {
+                const error = 'error' in parseResult ? parseResult.error : 'Unknown error';
+                const errorMessage = (0, zod_compat_js_1.getParseErrorMessage)(error);
+                // Log warning but don't throw - allow schema mismatches
+                console.warn(`[MCP SDK Patch] Output validation warning: Invalid structured content for tool ${toolName}: ${errorMessage}`);
+                // Keep the structuredContent despite validation failure
+            }
         }
     }
